"Testing reusable takeaway containers|Environment|Environmental science students review a reusable-container trial. Counting boxes returned seems straightforward, but their tutor asks whether people actually reused them before returning them. A deposit may increase returns while adding travel or washing costs. The group decides that the evaluation must consider these costs instead of describing every returned container as an environmental saving.|They will weigh empty containers before the trial and record washing cycles at the collection point. Customer interviews ask about extra journeys, but participants are not asked to calculate their own carbon footprints. A damaged box is recorded separately from a lost one. The tutor recommends reporting a range of estimates because energy use changes with washing temperature and how full the machine is.|The return incentive=deposit;The deposit amount=3;The first measurement=empty weight;The cleaning record=washing cycles;The interview topic=extra journeys;The separate category=damaged boxes;The variable setting=water temperature;The sample outlet=student canteen;The estimate format=range;The trial duration=21~days",
"Developing a wildlife microphone protocol|Science|A biology team asks its supervisor about leaving microphones in a woodland. One student proposes counting every recorded call as an animal, but the supervisor explains that a single bird may call repeatedly. The second student suggests recording the proportion of intervals with calls instead. This can describe activity without pretending to count distinct individuals.|Microphones are tested side by side before deployment so differences in sensitivity are known. Heavy rain can mask calls, and the team logs weather rather than quietly removing all wet days. Files receive location codes rather than names of nearby residents. The supervisor asks for a retention rule because unattended microphones may occasionally record human conversations as well as wildlife.|The outcome=active intervals;The calibration=side-by-side test;The masking condition=heavy rain;The file identifier=location code;The privacy risk=human conversation;The interval length=5~minutes;The sampling time=dawn;The microphone height=2~metres;The storage rule=restricted access;The deletion deadline=30~days",
